## NINEONELABS `no-loop-filter-rect` Component Analysis

I've thoroughly explored the codebase and found comprehensive information about the `no-loop-filter-rect` component. Here are my findings:

---

### 1. SCSS Component File

**Location:** `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\resource\scss\components\_loop-filter-rect.scss`

This is a pulsing 2x2 grid animation component:

```scss
@keyframes no-loop-filter-rect-pulse {
  0%, 18%, 100% {
    opacity: 0.16;
  }
  30%, 48% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}

.no-loop-filter-rect {
  --loop-filter-delay-base: 0s;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  gap: 0;
  flex-shrink: 0;

  span {
    width: fluid(3, 5);
    height: fluid(3, 5);
    background: currentColor;
    opacity: 0.16;
    animation: no-loop-filter-rect-pulse 1.2s linear infinite;
  }

  span:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: calc(var(--loop-filter-delay-base) + 0s); }
  span:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: calc(var(--loop-filter-delay-base) + 0.18s); }
  span:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: calc(var(--loop-filter-delay-base) + 0.54s); }
  span:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: calc(var(--loop-filter-delay-base) + 0.36s); }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    span {
      animation: none;
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }
}
```

**Key Features:**
- 4 square elements (2x2 grid) that pulse in a staggered pattern
- Each element has a 1.2s animation cycle
- Staggered delays: 0s, 0.18s, 0.54s, 0.36s (creates a wave-like visual pattern)
- Uses CSS variable `--loop-filter-delay-base` for dynamic delay adjustment
- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion` for accessibility

---

### 2. Usage Locations

The component is used in **two main places**:

#### A. Drawer Badge (Works Count)

**Location:** `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\views\components\drawer.php` (lines 100-111)

```php
<?php if ($root->slug() === 'works'): ?>
<span class="no-drawer__badge" aria-label="작품 <?= (int) $worksCount ?>건">
    <?= corner_bracket_html('no-drawer__badge-corner no-corner-bracket--shine') ?>
    <span class="no-drawer__badge-inner">
        <span class="no-loop-filter-rect no-drawer__badge-rect" aria-hidden="true">
            <span></span>
            <span></span>
            <span></span>
            <span></span>
        </span>
        <span class="no-drawer__badge-count f-display-2"><?= (int) $worksCount ?></span>
    </span>
</span>
<?php endif; ?>
```

**Related Styles:** `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\resource\scss\layouts\_drawer.scss` (lines 292-361)

```scss
&__badge {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  min-height: fluid(40, 46);
  padding: fluid(8, 10) fluid(12, 14);
  border: 1px solid var(--clr-border-weak);
  background: transparent;
  --corner-bracket-size: 10px;
  color: var(--clr-text-desc);
  transition: border-color var(--transition-default), background-color var(--transition-default), 
              transform var(--transition-default), color var(--transition-default);
}

&__badge-rect {
  position: relative;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* Hover states */
&__gnb-item:hover &__badge,
&__gnb-item:focus-within &__badge {
  border-color: var(--clr-border-default);
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--clr-border-weak) 12%, transparent);
  transform: translateY(-2px);
  color: var(--clr-text-title);
}

&__gnb-item:hover &__badge-rect span,
&__gnb-item:focus-within &__badge-rect span {
  opacity: 0.9;
}
```

#### B. Contact Wizard Overview

**Location:** `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\resource\ts\ui\ContactWizard.ts` (lines 886-896)

```typescript
private _createOverviewRect(): HTMLElement {
  const rect = document.createElement("span");
  rect.className = "no-loop-filter-rect no-wizard-overview__rect";
  rect.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");

  for (let index = 0; index < 4; index += 1) {
    rect.append(document.createElement("span"));
  }

  return rect;
}
```

The component creates 4 child spans dynamically and applies the `no-loop-filter-rect` class for animated step indicators in the multi-step wizard.

---

### 3. TypeScript Drawer Integration

**Location:** `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs\resource\ts\ui\Drawer.ts`

Key features:
- Handles drawer open/close transitions with `BlockOverlay` integration
- Uses `TextReveal` for staggered text masking animation
- Manages reveal groups with sequential delays
- Implements magnetic corner tracking on links (via `MagneticCornerTracker`)
- Supports Escape key to close drawer
- Syncs navigation active states

---

### 4. Interactive Components with Hover Animations

The codebase contains multiple interactive UI components that use `mouseenter`/`mouseleave` events:

| Component | File | Pattern |
|-----------|------|---------|
| **MagneticCornerTracker** | `Button.ts` (lines 422-437) | Draws animated corner SVG arms with GSAP on hover, elastic easing on leave |
| **WhySkillPreview** | `WhySkillPreview.ts` (lines 102-103) | Video preview switching with cinematic transitions |
| **ImagePreview** | `ImagePreview.ts` (lines 114-116) | Image follows cursor with throttled mousemove |
| **CharBtn** | `CharBtn.ts` (lines 61-62) | Character flip animation on hover using GSAP |
| **Marquee** | `Marquee.ts` (lines 60-61) | Playback control on hover |

---

### 5. getBoundingClientRect Usage

Found in 12 files, primarily for:
- **ContactWizard.ts** (lines 482-486): Scroll syncing of overview list items
- **ImagePreview.ts** (line 137): Position calculation relative to hover target
- **Button.ts** (MagneticCornerTracker): Measuring element bounds for corner tracking
- **ObserveManager.ts**: Viewport observation for animations
- **WhySkillPreview.ts** (line 137): Vertical positioning of preview element

---

### 6. Animation Pattern Architecture

**Key GSAP Usage Patterns:**
- GSAP is dynamically imported via `(window as WindowWithGsap).gsap`
- Tweens are killed and overwritten to prevent conflicts
- Stagger values for sequential animations
- Ease functions like `power3.out`, `elastic.out(1,.5)`, `ease-smooth`

**CSS Variable System:**
- `--loop-filter-delay-base`: Used to adjust animation timing dynamically
- `--transition-default`, `--transition-fast`: Global transition durations
- `--clr-*`: Semantic color variables for theming

---

### 7. Directory Structure Summary

**UI Components** (`resource/ts/ui/`):
- `Drawer.ts` - Full-screen menu with text reveal
- `ContactWizard.ts` - Multi-step form with chip animations
- `Panel.ts` - Progress visualization
- `BlockOverlay.ts` - Transition overlay
- `WorkCard.ts`, `WorkModal.ts` - Work preview modals
- `Header.ts`, `HudPanel.ts` - Navigation headers
- `Dropdown.ts` - Menu dropdown
- `IntroCanvas.ts`, `IntroOverlay.ts` - Intro screen

---

### 8. Component Creation Pattern

All interactive components follow this pattern:
1. Static `init()` method discovers DOM elements
2. Event listeners attached via `addEventListener()`
3. Cleanup in `dispose()` with `removeEventListener()`
4. Use of `requestAnimationFrame()` or `FrameScheduler` for RAF batching
5. Proper memory management with `WeakMap` for element-to-data associations

The `no-loop-filter-rect` component is a fundamental animated indicator used to signal active/processing states, with the CSS variable system allowing dynamic animation offset adjustments via JavaScript when needed.

